1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,203
You did your taxes, and you owe.

2
00:00:02,623 --> 00:00:06,936
Before you reach for a credit card, let's compare the options, with real numbers.

3
00:00:07,356 --> 00:00:12,412
Our example: a $2,400 tax bill, and $450 a month to put toward it.

4
00:00:13,182 --> 00:00:15,616
Rule number one comes before any of the math.

5
00:00:16,386 --> 00:00:18,590
File on time, even if you can't pay.

6
00:00:19,010 --> 00:00:32,561
The penalty for filing late is usually much bigger than for paying late: generally 5% of the unpaid tax per month, versus 0.5%. On $2,400, that's about $120 a month, versus $12.

7
00:00:32,981 --> 00:00:36,471
So file by the deadline no matter what. Then pick how to pay.

8
00:00:37,241 --> 00:00:39,363
Option one. Put it on a credit card.

9
00:00:39,783 --> 00:00:52,247
Card payment processors charge a fee, often around 2%: about $45 here. Then 24% interest. Paying $450 a month, it's about $215 in total.

10
00:00:53,017 --> 00:00:55,366
Option two. An IRS payment plan.

11
00:00:55,786 --> 00:01:07,883
If you can pay within 180 days, the IRS short-term plan has no setup fee. You still owe interest (7% a year as of late 2026) plus the small late-payment penalty.

12
00:01:08,303 --> 00:01:12,063
Same six months. About $86 instead of $215.

13
00:01:12,483 --> 00:01:23,081
Longer plans exist too, with a setup fee that's lower if you apply online with automatic payments. Rates and fees change, so check IRS.gov before you apply.

14
00:01:23,851 --> 00:01:25,849
And option three. Don't owe next year.

15
00:01:26,269 --> 00:01:37,444
Owing usually means too little was withheld. Adjust your W-4 so a little more comes out of each check: $2,400 over 26 paychecks is about $92 each.

16
00:01:37,864 --> 00:01:43,856
Freelance or side income? Set the tax aside every time you're paid. Episode thirty-one covers it.

17
00:01:44,626 --> 00:01:52,008
This is general education, not tax advice. The Paycheck Planner in the description fits the payment plan into your paychecks.

18
00:01:52,428 --> 00:01:55,184
Subscribe for more money math, with real numbers.
